Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 03:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] server: PS5: the desktop window can be made the foreground.

With the PS5 user driver no explorer owns the desktop window: get_desktop_window asks the server to create it, and
the server detaches it from every thread, so make_window_foreground refused it and
SetForegroundWindow(GetDesktopWindow()) failed. Windows allows it, and on the PC explorer's thread owns the desktop
and the call succeeds. A probe on the Pro (fgprobe-pro-01, 2026-10-28) showed the console's refusal; Wine's d3d9
tests use the call to take the focus from a fullscreen device (device.c:5234 and 12142, d3d9ex.c:3629), and the
activation and focus checks that follow it failed on the console too. The thread-less desktop is now made the
foreground for the caller, as each process already treats it as its own (WND_DESKTOP, patch 0410): no window stays
active and the caller's windows get WM_ACTIVATEAPP, as on Windows. On the Pro, with patch 2152, the console-only lines
went from 63 to 51 (x86_64) and 50 (i386) in device and from 42 to 32 in d3d9ex in both builds.
---
--- a/server/window.c
+++ b/server/window.c
@@ -1205,6 +1205,16 @@
 {
     struct window *win = get_user_object( window, NTUSER_OBJ_WINDOW );
 
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    /* No explorer owns the PS5 desktop (get_desktop_window creates it detached), and each process treats it as its
+     * own (WND_DESKTOP): making it the foreground, as Windows allows, leaves no window active for the caller. */
+    if (win && !win->thread && win->desktop == desktop && win == desktop->top_window)
+    {
+        *is_desktop = 1;
+        *set_foreground = 1;
+        return (struct thread *)grab_object( current );
+    }
+#endif
     if (!win || !win->thread || win->desktop != desktop) return NULL;
     if ((win->style & (WS_POPUP | WS_CHILD)) == WS_CHILD) return NULL;
     *is_desktop = win == win->desktop->top_window;
